    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0274" n="1108" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/230a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Norway</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schmedeman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-04T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 4, 1918—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>201. Department has been advised by British Ambassador that your British
                    colleague has been instructed as soon as you have received similar instructions
                    to present a note to the Norwegian Government stating that “providing a
                    satisfactory arrangement with the United States and the Allies is concluded,
                    Norway will receive rations estimated to satisfy her legitimate
                    requirements.”</p>
                <p>Department and War Trade Board approve of these instructions and you are
                    authorized to communicate to the Norwegian Government the substance thereof,
                    provided you deem the present moment an opportune one.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
